# smbtorture tests the server must pass, one full test ID per line, as
# printed by `smbtorture --list` from the Samba version pinned in test/Dockerfile.
#
# Left out on purpose:
# - smb2.credits: expects Samba's 8192 credits; this server grants 256.
# - smb2.lease and smb2.durable-v2-open: open one file from several clients,
#   or need oplocks, V1 leases, persistent handles or a 300 s durable cap.
# - smb2.dir.modify: names files in another case; this share is case-sensitive.
# - smb2.rename.rename_dir_openfile: expects renaming a directory with an open
#   file to fail; opens here follow the inode, so the rename is allowed.
# - smb2.compound.invalid1, invalid2 and invalid4: send a first request marked
#   related, a session that differs from the encryption header, or an unknown
#   command; the server ends the connection instead of answering.
# - smb2.rw.invalid: expects Windows' 16 TB file size limit and DISK_FULL.
# - smb2.dir.large-files, smb2.dir.sorted and
#   smb2.compound_find.compound_find_close: create 2000 to 5000 files and run
#   for minutes; smb2.dir.many covers large listings.
# - smb2.lock and smb2.create.brlocked: there are no range locks; LOCK answers
#   NOT_SUPPORTED.
smb2.getinfo.granted.granted
smb2.read.eof.eof
smb2.read.dir.dir
smb2.read.access.access
smb2.dir.find.find
smb2.dir.fixed.fixed
smb2.dir.many.many
smb2.compound.related1.related1
smb2.compound.related2.related2
smb2.compound.related5.related5
smb2.compound.unrelated1.unrelated1
smb2.compound.invalid3.invalid3
smb2.compound.create-write-close.create-write-close
smb2.compound_find.compound_find_related.compound_find_related
smb2.compound_find.compound_find_unrelated.compound_find_unrelated
smb2.compound_async.flush_close.flush_close
smb2.compound_async.flush_flush.flush_flush
smb2.rename.simple.simple
smb2.rename.simple_nodelete.simple_nodelete
smb2.rename.no_sharing.no_sharing
smb2.rename.msword.msword
smb2.rename.rename_dir_bench.rename_dir_bench
smb2.rename.close-full-information.close-full-information
smb2.rw.rw1.rw1
smb2.rw.rw2.rw2
smb2.sharemode.sharemode-access.sharemode-access
smb2.sharemode.access-sharemode.access-sharemode
smb2.create.multi.multi
smb2.create.open.open
smb2.create.delete.delete
smb2.create.mkdir-dup.mkdir-dup
smb2.create.dir-alloc-size.dir-alloc-size
smb2.create.dosattr_tmp_dir.dosattr_tmp_dir
smb2.create.bench-path-contention-shared.bench-path-contention-shared
